^h1{Places to visit}
^connection{https://www.bekonscot.co.uk/}{Bekonscot}{The famous Bekonscot Model Village with G1 model railway}
^connection{https://www.hara-mrm.com/english/}{Hara Model Train Museum}{A large model railway museum in Yokohama, Japan}
^connection{https://www.technik-museum.de/en/}{Technik Museum}{Sinsheim, Germany.}

^h1{Other gauge and scale societies}
^connection{https://www.gaugeoguild.com/}{The Gauge ‘O’ Guild}{All forms of railway modelling in 7mm. scale and on 0 gauge track.}
^connection{https://www.16mm.org.uk/}{The 16mm Association}{The Association of 16mm Narrow Gauge Modellers.}
^connection{https://gscalesociety.com/}{The G-Scale Society}{Mainly narrow gauge modelling on G1 45mm track.}
^connection{https://n25ga.org/}{The National 2½ Inch Gauge Association}{2.5″gauge model engineering.}
^connection{https://www.gauge3.org.uk/}{The Gauge 3 Society}{The 2.5″ gauge large-scale scenic model railway group.}
^connection{https://traincollector.co.uk/}{The Train Collectors Society}{For those interested in all makes and gauges of toy and model trains.}

^h1{Modelling and engineering societies}
^connection{https://suttonmec.org/}{Sutton Model Engineering Club}{Sutton has an extensive G1 track}
^connection{https://www.swissmodelcarclub.ch/gruppe_eiwi_eisenbahn_witterswil}{EiWi G1 Railway}{Swiss Model Car Club Gauge 1 group and track at  Witterswil}
^connection{http://havebane.dk/}{Gauge One in Denmark}{David and Axel Clement’s fine G1 railway}
^connection{https://psgrs.org/}{Puget Sound Garden Railway Society}{}
^connection{https://sidestreet.info/railways/gr.home.html}{Sidestreet Bannerworks}{Marc Horowitz' site, including ten years of'Locomotive of the month'}

